## 75. Sort Colors

### Approach
I Used Three Pointers : `left`, `current`, and `right`.

--  0 → swap with `left`, then move `left` and `current`.
--  1 → just move `current`.
--  2 → swap with `right`, move `right`, but don't move current because the swapped element still needs to be checked.

This sorts the array in-place and one-pass algorithm
Time = O(n) 
Space = O(1)

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {

    // Helper swap function for quick swapping
    void swap(int[] nums, int left, int right) {
        int temp = nums[left];
        nums[left] = nums[right];
        nums[right] = temp;
    }

    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int left = 0;
        int current = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;
        while (current <= right) {
            if (nums[current] == 0) {
                swap(nums, left, current);
                left++;
                current++;
            } else if (nums[current] == 1) {
                current++;
            } else {
                swap(nums, current, right);
                right--;
            }
        }
    }
}
